course: dictionary
lesson: 5502
title: Lay: to put down, or the past of lie
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Lay is a small word with more than one job. Most of the time it means to put something down carefully, often flat. «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon.» Here laid means the plates and cutlery have been put out ready for a meal.
explain: Lay can also be about animals. «Some rare birds lay a second egg if the first is taken.» A bird lays an egg when the egg comes out of her body. Look at the words around lay to find its meaning: eggs, birds and taken tell you it is about making eggs.
explain: Watch out for lay as the past of lie, which means to rest flat. «He lay on the grass» means he rested flat on the grass, not that he put something down. Ask yourself: is there an object being placed? If yes, lay means to put down. If someone is resting, it is probably lie.
explain: Lay also appears in phrases like lay the table, lay out and lay off. These give extra clues. Lay out means arrange, and lay off means stop, so always try the meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Lay means to put something down carefully, often flat.
fact: «Lay» is also the past form of «lie», which means to rest flat, as in «He lay on the grass».
fact: Lay is a verb, and its forms are lay, lays, laid and laying. Laid is the past form of lay.
fact: «Laid» can describe a table that has been set for a meal, with plates, knives, forks and spoons.
fact: A check you can use is to swap in put down. If the sentence still makes sense, lay is probably the right meaning.
exercise: «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon.» What does laid mean here? | Cleaned after a meal | *Set out ready for a meal | Hidden under a cloth | Lying flat on the floor
exercise: «Some rare birds lay a second egg if the first is taken.» What does lay mean here? | To hatch chicks | *To produce an egg from the body | To rest flat | To put a bird in a cage
exercise: In «He lay on the grass», lay is the past form of which word? | leap | lay | lend | *lie
test: «The bee hummingbird lays eggs the size of a pea.» What size are its eggs? | The size of a bee | *The size of a pea | The size of a football | The size of a house
test: To lay bricks means to put them in place to build a wall. In this case, what does lay mean? | *To put in position | To throw away | To rest flat | To hatch
exam: «Water molecules pull tightly on each other at the surface, and a paperclip laid gently can float.» What does laid mean here? | Stretched out to dry | Thrown hard | *Put down carefully | Dropped from a height
